## 📌 Coding Patterns & Conventions
- **Django Migrations**: Always specify dependencies for migrations. Never delete migration files unless performing a squashed migration.
- **REST APIs**: Utilize Django REST Framework's class-based views (specifically ModelViewSet) and document them correctly using `drf-spectacular` annotations.
- **Type Hints**: Standard Python 3.13 type hinting is required for all new functions/classes.
- **Error Handling**: Follow structured logging patterns. Log messages using standard levels (TRACE/DEBUG/INFO/WARNING/ERROR). Keep console handlers verbose.
- **Task Safety**: When writing Celery background tasks, use locking mechanisms where appropriate to avoid race conditions during concurrent data processing (e.g., EPG ingestion, channel stats).
